                  <provenance type="#c" cert="low" source="3264"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_268">Hyde (Hida, formerly
                        New Minster, Winchester), Hampshire. Benedictine abbey of Holy Trinity, St
                        Mary the Virgin, and St Peter</orgName><p>Ascribed by H.R. Luard, who
                        published the Annals in Annales monastici, RS 2, to St Swithin's,
                        Winchester. For the attribution to Hyde see Eng. Hist. Rev. 49 (1934), pp.
                        85ff.</p><p>Fols. 70r--87r are said to be in the same hand as CCCC 339, vol.
                        1: Howlettt considered both autograph of Richard Devizes.</p></provenance>
               <provenance cert="low" source="5743"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_437">Winchester, Hampshire.
                        Benedictine cathedral priory of St Peter, St Paul, and St Swithun</orgName><p>Provenance suggested by contents, but perhaps from Hyde (q. v.)
                        rather than Old Minster. Fols. 70--87 in same hand as Cambrige, CCC 339, i.
                        D. Howlett, Chronicon of the reigns of Stephen, RS, considered both MSS.
                        autographs of R. of Devizes.</p></provenance>
